Subject: Recommend the unpackers for the formats games ship in

Debian only Suggests them, so apt installs none and game-data-packager stops at the first CD
cabinet, GOG installer or archive ("cannot unpack ...: tool ... is not installed"). Walnut
imports game data from discs, installers and archives, so the common ones come along:
innoextract (GOG's setup_*.exe), unshield (InstallShield cabinets, e.g. RollerCoaster Tycoon 2's
CD), cabextract (Microsoft cabinets), 7zip, lhasa (LHA archives, e.g. Quake 1.06's resource.1,
which a Quake 1.01 CD needs, and the Master Levels' master.exe) and unzip. unar stays a Suggests
(it pulls in GNUstep), xorriso too (only three games read an ISO through it).

Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/debian/control b/debian/control
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -38,22 +38,24 @@ Depends:
  ${misc:Depends},
  ${python3:Depends},
 Recommends:
+ 7zip,
+ cabextract,
  game-data-packager-runtime (>= ${source:Version}),
+ innoextract,
+ lhasa | jlha-utils | lzh-archiver,
+ unshield,
+ unzip,
 Suggests:
- 7zip,
  arj,
  binutils,
- cabextract,
  cdparanoia,
  dynamite,
  gcc,
  gdebi | gdebi-kde,
  gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0,
- innoextract,
  lame,
  lgc-pg,
  lgogdownloader,
- lhasa | jlha-utils | lzh-archiver,
  make,
  pkexec,
  python3-gi,
@@ -64,8 +66,6 @@ Suggests:
  unace-nonfree,
  unar,
  unrar,
- unshield,
- unzip,
  vorbis-tools,
  xdelta,
  xdelta3,
